 CDESCRIBE 2 26 62 The DISPLAY workspace contains three functions:             ø
                                                                               ø
 Z½DISPLAY  X   Z is a character array which pictorially                       ø
       represents the array X.  DISPLAY uses                         box       ø
  drawing characters.                                                          ø
                                    Z½DISPLAYC X   Z is a character arra       ø
 y which pictorially                      represents the array X.  DISPL       ø
 AYC uses                        characters from the APL2 character set.       ø
                                                                       Z       ø
 ½DISPLAYG X   Equivalent to DISPLAY.  Supplied for                            ø
      compatibility with other APL2 platforms.                                 ø
                                            The following characters are       ø
  used to convey shape information:    ¸ or Ç indicates a dimension of a       ø
 t least one,                 é or è indicates a dimension of zero,            ø
                     (none of the above) indicates no dimension.               ø
                                                                      Th       ø
 e following characters are used to convey type information:     ~ indic       ø
 ates numeric,                                          + indicates mixe       ø
 d,                                            î indicates nested,             ø
                                      _ indicates a scalar character whi       ø
 ch is at the same depth       as non-scalar arrays.                           ø
                    (none of the above) indicates a character array whic       ø
Xh is        not a simple scalar.                                              ø
